WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.849
Start a supervised analysis with a synthetic
incident. Give it a useful title and

00:00:05.849 --> 00:00:11.843
separate observations from hypotheses. In
this example, database connections appear

00:00:11.843 --> 00:00:17.548
exhausted, but a cause has not yet been
established. Specify that no restart or

00:00:17.548 --> 00:00:20.075
configuration change is authorized.

00:00:20.903 --> 00:00:26.882
After submitting, inspect the proposal and
the status of the investigation. Check the

00:00:26.882 --> 00:00:32.580
quoted runbook passages, missing evidence
and the limits of the local consistency

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:38.419
review. A plausible explanation is not an
observed root cause. This tutorial uses a

00:00:38.419 --> 00:00:42.428
deterministic response to make the sequence
reproducible.

00:00:43.244 --> 00:00:49.228
Open the rejection dialog when the proposal
is not sufficiently supported. Read the

00:00:49.228 --> 00:00:55.429
decision before confirming it. Approval or
rejection records a human decision; it does

00:00:55.429 --> 00:01:01.414
not execute remediation commands. A refused
proposal must remain visible instead of

00:01:01.414 --> 00:01:05.019
being silently rewritten as an approved
diagnosis.

00:01:05.866 --> 00:01:11.796
Return to the analysis history and reopen
the completed record. Review its status,

00:01:11.796 --> 00:01:17.871
evidence and export options. Share an export
only after checking that it contains no

00:01:17.871 --> 00:01:24.018
secrets or client data beyond its intended
audience. Use a separate analysis when new

00:01:24.018 --> 00:01:26.766
observations change the investigation.
